{
    "id": "project-context-explainer",
    "question": "How does Footnote's project context integration work?",
    "response": {
        "action": "message",
        "message": "Footnote's project context integration lets it answer questions about Footnote from approved project documents rather than a web search. It reads the local allowlist in `.footnote/context-files`, splits approved documents into excerpts, and uses a separately configured embedding model to find the relevant ones for a question [1](https://github.com/footnote-ai/footnote/blob/65c3405b411f4a34e484f5a7e4c52c1d51eae8f9/docs/architecture/context-integrations/project-context.md).\n\nThe integration supports explanations, onboarding, contribution, and discovery—for example, answering \"How does Footnote work?\" or \"Where should I start contributing?\" It can also pair those documents with live GitHub results when the question concerns Footnote's current state [2](https://github.com/footnote-ai/footnote/blob/65c3405b411f4a34e484f5a7e4c52c1d51eae8f9/docs/architecture/context-integrations/project-context.md). When the local index content still matches, it reuses the cached index, and it serves `project_context` without TrustGraph; TrustGraph remains the longer-term external retrieval option [3](https://github.com/footnote-ai/footnote/blob/65c3405b411f4a34e484f5a7e4c52c1d51eae8f9/docs/status/repository-context-status.md).\n\nProject documents are treated strictly as source material, not instructions. Retrieved excerpts are marked `UNTRUSTED PROJECT CONTEXT` and the model is instructed not to follow any directives found in them; the context step returns these excerpts as bounded Evidence, kept separate from trusted instructions and projected as user-level advisory data [4](https://github.com/footnote-ai/footnote/blob/65c3405b411f4a34e484f5a7e4c52c1d51eae8f9/docs/architecture/context-integrations/project-context.md). The broader goal is to let a repository define which files Footnote may use, then make loading them into TrustGraph and using them during chat straightforward—with user-facing language like \"repository context,\" \"connect TrustGraph,\" \"review files,\" \"load context,\" and \"refresh context\" [5](https://github.com/footnote-ai/footnote/blob/65c3405b411f4a34e484f5a7e4c52c1d51eae8f9/docs/status/repository-context-status.md). Note that the project is pre-1.0 and changing quickly [6](https://github.com/footnote-ai/footnote/blob/65c3405b411f4a34e484f5a7e4c52c1d51eae8f9/AGENTS.md).",
        "modality": "text",
